course: dictionary
lesson: 9779
title: Surplus: what is left over
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A surplus is the extra amount left over after you have what you need. If a class has 26 pencils and needs only 21, the surplus is 5 pencils. «The farm had a surplus of eggs, so it sold the extra at the market.» The farm had more eggs than it needed, so the extra eggs were left over.
explain: Surplus can be a noun or an adjective. As a noun, it is the extra amount: «a surplus of food». As an adjective, it describes something extra: «surplus food» means food that is not needed. Look at the words around it to see which one it is.
explain: Money can have a surplus too. A budget surplus is when more money comes in than goes out. Ask yourself: is there more left over than is needed? If yes, that is a surplus.
fact: Surplus means an extra amount that is more than what is needed.
fact: «Surplus food» means food that is extra and not needed.
fact: You can work out a surplus with this sum: what there is minus what is needed.
fact: A farm with a surplus of food can sell it or trade it with other people.
fact: In Chinese, «yú» means fish and sounds like the word for surplus, so families eat a whole fish at New Year to wish for plenty every year.
exercise: «The farm had a surplus of eggs, so it sold the extra.» What does surplus mean here? | Broken | *Extra, more than needed | Empty and bare | Very small
exercise: A class has 26 pencils and needs 21. What is the surplus? | 21 | *5 | 47 | 26
exercise: Ben says, «The food bank has surplus food.» Find and copy the word that means extra. | has | bank | *surplus | food
test: What is a budget surplus? | When more money goes out than comes in | When you lose your wallet | *When more money comes in than goes out | When there is no money at all
test: Why do families eat a whole fish at New Year, since «yú» sounds like surplus? | Because fish is the cheapest food | *To wish for plenty every year | Because they have no other food | To make the kitchen smell nice
exam: After Sam's birthday there was a surplus of cake, so the family gave the extra to the neighbours. What does surplus mean? | Not enough to share | Dirty and spoiled | A tiny crumb | *More than they needed
